wumpus programs vendored for integration testing
==================================================

`.in` files are wumpus programs sourced verbatim from the upstream
wumpus repo's `examples/` directory:

  https://github.com/m-ender/wumpus
  copy is at internal/integrationtest/testdata/gems/wumpus/

each `.in` is the corresponding `<name>.wumpus` from `examples/`,
renamed so the goruby esolang test harness picks them up. `.expected`
files were generated by running

  ruby internal/integrationtest/testdata/gems/wumpus/wumpus.rb \
       <fixture>.in </dev/null > <fixture>.expected

under MRI 2.6.10.

omitted programs and why
------------------------

- kolakoski.wumpus -- prints the kolakoski sequence forever, both mri
  and goruby hit a timeout. no useful baseline.
- wumpus.wumpus -- the namesake "hunt the wumpus" game uses
  Kernel#rand; output is non-deterministic and won't match mri's
  random sequence run-to-run. could be revisited once a seeded
  randomness mode is wired.

